# Source and status audit: 30001075

Checked 2026-09-30 UTC. This is a limited literature search, not a historical-priority certificate.

## Exact primary sources

- [OWR 44/2008, section 13, p. 2552](https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46191): Conjecture 4 is the measure-zero claim. Tangency means meeting the convex set while lying in a supporting plane. Conjecture 3 is a stronger manifold-cover claim. Neither smoothness nor generic position is present. The report records nowhere density, expressly warning that this does not imply measure zero.
- [Demouth, 2008 thesis](https://theses.hal.science/tel-00342717/document): the complete 157-page PDF was downloaded; chapter 4 pp. 48–66 inspected. Definition on p.48 assumes closed convex sets. Theorem3 p.51 and Lemma20 p.66 prove nowhere density. Lemmas17–19 pp.61–66 use local geometry and topological stability, not a Lebesgue-null proof. The candidate does not use these lemmas.
- Demouth–Goaoc, *Topological changes in the apparent contour of convex sets*, 2008 manuscript, cited by OWR. A separately published final version was not located. The thesis supplies the inspected original argument; do not claim that an independently retrieved manuscript PDF was inspected.

## Later-source search

- [Goaoc current research page](https://members.loria.fr/Xavier.Goaoc/) and its complete publication list were searched. Topics include line transversals, pinning, spheres, polyhedra, and visibility. No exact resolution located.
- [Demouth publication list maintained by Gamble](https://gamble.loria.fr/publications/publications_Julien_Demouth.html) links the thesis and the 2009 workshop paper *Computing Direct Shadows Cast by Convex Polyhedra*. This is polyhedral and cites the topological manuscript; it is not a resolution for arbitrary convex sets.
- Search terms included the exact manuscript/conjecture titles, “three convex sets” with “measure”, “visual event surfaces” with “measure zero”, “common tangents” with “Lipschitz” and “rectifiable”, and “tritangent” with recent years. No exact later resolution located. Algebraic/smooth-generic visibility results cannot establish the nonsmooth claim.

## Prior-attempt and duplicate gate

The pinned upstream dataset has one record with this exact problem code and no associated research report. The local all-record scan found no duplicate of this conjecture. The main queue was queued, 0/5; main state was empty; the history had no target entry. Related-target groups had no match. The full recursive main tree was not truncated and contained no target attempt. The all-state PR inventory through PR12 contained no previous tangent-locus attempt. The checks include invalidated/closed earlier work to the extent represented by these artifacts. Main's unrelated tangent-named files were in other research projects and did not concern this target.

## Scope of the proposed result

The candidate proves only Conjecture4, through a null swept Jacobian on Lipschitz two-parameter line covers. This does not yield a countable cover of the locus by smooth 2-manifolds. Its reduction extends from compact convex sets to arbitrary convex sets, including nonclosed ones, without presupposing their measurability. The current classification is candidate awaiting separate adversarial review. Priority remains unconfirmed even if the mathematics passes.
